15068427,2025-08-04,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am submitting this formal complaint to dispute several inaccurate, outdated, and harmful pieces of information being reported on my credit profile by XXXX XXXX and the credit bureaus. These inaccuracies have caused me ongoing emotional distress, financial hardship, and reputational damage. Despite multiple attempts to resolve this directly with the credit reporting agencies and the furnisher, these issues remain unresolved. 
Addresses ( Wrong/Unauthorized ) XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, FL XXXX XXXX : I have never resided at this location nor have I used this address in any financial, personal, or employment capacity Law : FCRA 1681e ( b ) requires credit bureaus to follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy Story : This address appeared on my report without my knowledge, likely due to file mixing or identity theft. Due to this, Ive been questioned by lenders and job agencies who believe I have undisclosed residences. This misreporting continues to harm my credibility, delay approvals, and interfere with my life. I demand its permanent removal. 
XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX This is not now, nor has it ever been, my residence Law : FCRA 1681i ( a ) I have the right to dispute incomplete or inaccurate information Story : Ive never received mail, bills, or credit offers at this address. I suspect identity confusion or administrative error. This address being tied to my identity misrepresents my location history and damages my credit profile. 
