15083787,2025-08-06,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing this formal complaint to bring to the attention of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) a series of serious violations of my consumer rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). Despite my numerous attempts to dispute and resolve multiple inaccuracies, incorrect information continues to appear on my credit report, including false addresses, late payments that I did not incur, charge-off entries that were never properly validated, and several unauthorized hard inquiries that were made without my consent or permissible purpose. I have contacted the major credit reporting agencies ( Experian, XXXX, and XXXX  ) and the furnishers of these accounts, yet no valid proof or investigation results were provided. Therefore, I am requesting that the CFPB urgently intervene, initiate a full investigation, and compel the responsible parties to permanently delete these items from my credit report in accordance with the law. 
ADDRESS DISPUTES XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX  XXXX LAW : FCRA XXXX ( c ) ( XXXX ) ( XXXX ), XXXX ( A ), XXXX ISSUE : False Residential Data STORY : I have never lived at this address nor authorized any credit activity from this location. This information is incorrect and must be removed to preserve the accuracy of my profile. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX  XXXX LAW : FCRA XXXX ( c ) ( XXXX ) ( XXXX ), XXXX ( A ), XXXX ISSUE : Invalid Address on File STORY : This address does not belong to me and may have been erroneously associated with my file. It should be deleted promptly to ensure my credit report reflects only verifiable data. 

