15117002,2025-08-06,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against JPMorgan Chase Bank regarding their mishandling of a Regulation E error resolution process related to several unauthorized transactions on my debit card. 

Summary of Events : On XX/XX/year>, I traveled to XXXX XXXX, XXXX. Upon arrival, I used my Chase debit card once to withdraw cash from an ATM located inside the airport. That was the last time I used the card. On XX/XX/year>, I discovered that my debit card was missing and, upon checking my account, found five unauthorized charges, each in the amount of {$370.00} ( XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX and XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX ), totaling {$1800.00}. These transactions occurred in XXXX, a city I never visited during my trip. 

I immediately reported my debit card as lost/stolen and filed a fraud claim with Chase. Despite submitting documentation to support my caseincluding credit card transactions and XXXX XXXX receipts showing my location was nowhere near XXXXChase denied my claim, stating that the transactions were considered "" authorized. '' I then requested the documentation Chase relied upon to make their determination, as is my right under 12 CFR 1005.11 ( d ) of Regulation E. Instead of providing this documentation, I received a generic letter stating : Upon our review your claim was denied based on information available to us at the time of the decision and/or previous account activity. 

