15192459,2025-08-11,Vehicle loan or lease,Loan,Managing the loan or lease,Problem with fees charged,"SUMMARY OF COMPLAINT I, XXXX XXXX XXXX, suffered ascertainable economic damages as a direct and proximate result of NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE COMPANY 's misrepresentations, deceptive practices, misconduct, breach of contract, mail fraud, breach of privacy, insurance fraud, etc., including but not limited to paying excessive interest, loss of expected rebate benefits, and diminished value of the contract bargain. The causes of injury are further described therein : A. - MISREPRESENTATION OF ANNUAL PERCENTAGE RATE ( APR ), MISREPRESENTATION & DECEPTION 1. NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE COMPANY is a creditor as defined under the Truth in Lending Act ( TILA ), 15 U.S.C. 1602 ( g ), and the Texas Finance Code 348.001 ( 3 ), engaged in the business of financing motor vehicle purchases in the State of Texas.

2. On or about XX/XX/year>, I, XXXX XXXX XXXX entered into a Retail Installment Sales Contract ( RISC ) with NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE COMPANY for the financing of a motor vehicle. NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE COMPANY not only misrepresented that a "" down payment '' was required but al represented in the TILA disclosure statement that the Annual Percentage Rate ( APR ) for my loan was [ stated APR 7 %, to be repaid in [ XXXX ] monthly payments of $ [ XXXX ]. 

