NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE COMPANY 's conduct constitutes : A violation of The Consumer Law Group, P.C. and Regulation Z- which require clear and accurate disclosures about loan terms, costs, and fees. Failing to disclose the true nature of the GAP insurance or intentionally creating conditions for default violate transparency requirements.

A violation of the Federal Trade Commission Act ( FTC Act ) : This act prohibits unfair and deceptive acts or practices in commerce. The alleged scheme could be considered an unfair or deceptive practice under this act.

A violation of the Consumer Financial Protection Act ( CFPA ) : This act established the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ), which enforces consumer financial protection laws and regulations. The CFPB has taken action against companies engaging in unfair, deceptive, or abusive practices in auto loan servicing, including issues related to optional add-on products and payment misapplication, which are relevant to this scenario.

