Texas Department of Insurance ( .gov ). ( Currently requesting report. ) A violation of Texas Finance Code : This code regulates consumer loans, including interest computation methods and delinquency charges. Violations related to misapplying payments or charging excessive late fees are addressed under this code.

D. - ABUSE OF CAPITOL STOCK FOR AUTO LOANS & DECEPTION - Facts to support complaint Auto finance companies, including both banks and non-bank lenders, obtain funds to issue auto loans through various channels, one of which can be leveraging their own capital stock. XXXX XXXX, This involves using the company 's equity ( capital stock ) as a base to generate funds for lending or as a form of security in financial markets. 

Capital stock and loan financing - Definition : Capital stock represents the ownership shares of a company, representing its equity. These funds are contributed by investors who own a piece of the company.

Financing Operations : Auto finance companies utilize these capital funds to directly finance loans, operate their business, and/or use as a basis to issue debt or asset-backed securities ( ABS ).

Asset-Backed Securities ( ABS ) : Auto ABS are structured financial products where auto loans are bundled together and then sold to investors as securities. NAIC.

ABS and personal/financial information : Securitization Process : When auto loans are securitized and packaged into ABS, information about the underlying loans is included. Guggenheim Investments, Loan Data : This information includes details like loan amounts, interest rates, payment schedules, borrower demographics, and sometimes credit scores. NAIC, Disclosure Concerns : The use of this personal and financial information without explicit consent from consumers is where the issue arises, under data privacy and consumer protection laws.

