D. - RIGHT TO PUBLICITY Definition : The right of publicity ( ROP ) is an individual 's right to control and profit from the commercial use of their name, image, likeness, voice, or other identifying characteristics.

Commercial Value : The ROP has significant commercial value, especially for public figures, celebrities, or individuals whose identity is tied to a brand or product.

Property Right : Courts have recognized the ROP as a property right, meaning it can be owned, licensed, transferred, and even inherited, similar to other assets.

Financial instruments Definition : Financial instruments are contracts that represent a monetary value, such as stocks, bonds, loans, or derivatives.

