This is not in compliance with the FDCPA, which requires the debt collector not the original creditor to provide proof. 

Sunrise also claimed they had been attempting to contact me for months via phone and email. They admitted they had the wrong phone number, and I have received no emails, letters, or phone calls from them prior to my call today. This means they have not properly provided the required written notice of debt as required by FDCPA 809 ( a ) within 5 days of initial communication. 

When I inquired about a pay-for-delete arrangement, the representative was dismissive and refused to discuss any resolution that would result in deletion from my credit reports, offering only a reduced settlement instead. This is my right to negotiate, and their refusal to even consider written terms raises concerns about their good faith in resolving disputes. 

Additionally, Sunrise Credit Services continues to report this account to all three major credit bureaus without noting that it is disputed, which is a violation of FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 3 ).

I am requesting that the CFPB investigate the following : 1. Sunrise Credit Services failure to provide proper validation of the debt under FDCPA 809 ( b ).

2. Sunrise Credit Services failure to provide initial written notice of debt within the required timeframe under FDCPA 809 ( a ).

3. Sunrise Credit Services failure to update credit reporting to reflect the account as disputed in compliance with FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 3 ).

