15313619,2025-08-15,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Dear CFPB Investigator, I am submitting this formal complaint against [ Credit Bureau Name ] and certain furnishers of information for reporting, maintaining, and failing to correct multiple inaccurate and unauthorized entries on my credit file in direct violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), 15 U.S.C. 1681 et seq., and the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ). 
These inaccuracies have caused measurable harm, including reduced credit scores, higher interest rates, denial of credit opportunities, and reputational damage. The credit bureau has failed in its obligations to maintain maximum possible accuracy ( 1681e ( b ) ) and to conduct a reasonable reinvestigation of disputed items ( 1681i ). Several furnishers have also violated their duty under 1681s-2 ( a ) to avoid reporting information they know or should know is inaccurate. 
XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Address Issue : This address is not now, nor has it ever been, associated with me. 
Law : FCRA 1681c ( a ) ( 4 ) prohibits the inclusion of inaccurate address information in a credit report. 
Story : I have never lived, worked, or conducted any personal or financial activity at this location. Its presence on my credit file is misleading and could result in my being linked to debts, criminal records, or judgments that belong to someone else. This is especially concerning because inaccurate addresses are often an early indicator of identity theft. Every time I apply for credit or housing, the false appearance of this XXXX address undermines my credibility and forces me to explain to lenders why my report contains data that is simply not mine. This has caused embarrassment during loan applications and delays in approvals, wasting valuable time and resources. 
XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Address Issue : Incorrect historical address. 
Law : FCRA 1681i requires the credit bureau to investigate and delete unverifiable address records. 
Story : I have no personal or professional connection to this address. The fact that it is showing up on my credit report could link me to accounts or public records that are fraudulent. I have already had a mortgage lender question me about why I have multiple Michigan addresses when my documented history shows otherwise. This is humiliating and financially damaging, as I have lost potential opportunities due to the appearance of instability or deception in my file. 
XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Address Issue : False association. 
Law : FCRA 1681e ( b ) mandates maximum possible accuracy in consumer reports. 
Story : I have never lived in Texas at this location, yet your system reports it as part of my history. This is not only inaccurate but also dangerous, because it makes me appear to have lived across the country in unrelated states, potentially linking me to unpaid debts or court judgments in Texas that have nothing to do with me. When a bank underwriter sees this, they may suspect fraud or instability, both of which can result in application denial. 
TBOM/ASPIRE Account # XXXX High Balance : {$1300.00} Late Payment Issue : Payment history inaccurately reported as late. 
Law : FCRA 1681s-2 ( a ) prohibits furnishing information known to be inaccurate. 
Story : I maintain meticulous payment records, and they show that my payments were made on time. This false late payment entry paints me as an unreliable borrower, causing interest rate increases and loan denials. The harm is measurable my score has dropped, and I was recently denied an auto refinance offer as a direct result. 
XXXX Account # XXXX * High Balance : {$770.00} Late Payment * * Issue : False late payment reporting. 
Law : FCRA 1681e ( b ) and 1681i require accuracy and reinvestigation. 
