Immediately thereafter, the individual initiated XXXX ( XXXX ) unauthorized withdrawals from my USD wallet to this new bank account. The transactions were for the following amounts : {$4900.00} {$4900.00} {$4900.00} {$3000.00} On the same day, XX/XX/year>, as soon as I detected this activity, I immediately contacted Coinbase support to report the fraud. At the time of my report, all four withdrawal transactions were clearly in "" PENDING '' status. Following protocol, Coinbase then locked my account, supposedly to prevent further damage and stop the unauthorized activity. 

On XX/XX/year>, I received an official notification from the Coinbase team. In this communication, I was explicitly assured that the pending transactions would be canceled as part of the security procedure while my account remained locked. This communication gave me confidence that Coinbase had the situation under control and that my funds were safe. 

However, Coinbase completely failed to follow its own procedure and the assurance they provided me. Even though my account was continuously locked, Coinbase allowed all XXXX fraudulent transfers to complete, sending a total of {$17000.00} to the thief. 

My account remained locked and out of my control from XX/XX/year>, until XX/XX/year>. During this period, I was not offered a resolution or a refund for the funds I lost due to the company 's negligence. 

Key Failures by Coinbase : Failure of Timely Action : Coinbase failed to act on my fraud report in time to cancel the transfers, despite them being in a "" pending '' status and having a clear window of opportunity to do so. 

